.TH MMAP_MAP 3
.SH NAME
mmap_map \- map a region of a file into memory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "mmap.h"
.PP
.BI "char* mmap_map(fd_type " fd ", size_t " sz ", uint64 " offset ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mmap_map
creates a memory mapping of
.I sz
bytes from the file descriptor
.I fd
starting at
.I offset
.
On POSIX systems, this creates a private, read-write mapping using
.BR mmap (2).
On Windows, it uses
.BR CreateFileMapping (3)
and
.BR MapViewOfFile (3)
with
.B PAGE_WRITECOPY
semantics.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a pointer to the mapped memory on success, or NULL on failure.